Global Copper Deposit Analysis
An Integrated Data-Driven Framework for Deposit Classification, Pattern Discovery, and
Exploration Targeting
Overview
This project applies a reproducible, data-driven workflow to global copper deposit data in order to (a)
identify the features that distinguish the five dominant copper deposit types, (b) classify mineral occur
rences with machine learning, (c) mine mineral-assemblage and geochemical co-occurrence patterns, and
(d) map the spatio-temporal distribution of deposits to highlight under-explored regions and prospective
metallogenic belts.
Deposit types covered: porphyry, sediment-hosted, magmatic sulfide, volcanogenic massive
sulfide (VMS), and iron oxide-copper-gold (IOCG) — globally, from the Archean to the present.
Research Questions
• RQ1 — Diagnostic features: Which geological, geospatial, and mineralogical features most
effectively differentiate the five deposit types?
• RQ2—Predictive classification: Can a machine learning model accurately classify occurrences
into deposit types, outperforming traditional geological methods?
• RQ3 — Pattern discovery: How do mineral assemblages and geochemical signatures (Cu, Mo,
Au, Ag) co-occur, and what do these patterns reveal about metallogenic processes?
• RQ4 — Spatio-temporal targeting: What is the global spatial and temporal distribution of
copper deposits, and where are the under-explored regions or new metallogenic belts?
