Installation
git clonehttps://github.com/<your-username>/<repo-name>.git
cd<repo-name>
python-mvenv.venv&&source .venv/bin/activate #Windows:.venv\Scripts\activate
pip install-rrequirements.txt
Core dependencies: pandas, numpy, scikit-learn, xgboost, scipy, mlxtend (Apriori), networkx,
esda/pysal,geopandas,shap,matplotlib,seaborn.
GeneratedbyKimi.ai
Usage
# 1. Build the integrated dataset
python src/preprocessing/build_dataset.py
# 2. Run each research-question module
python src/features/diagnostic_features.py
# RQ1
python src/models/train_classifiers.py
# RQ2
python src/patterns/association_mining.py
# RQ3
python src/spatial/spatiotemporal_analysis.py # RQ4
Outputs (figures, tables, model artefacts) are written to results/.
Results
To be updated as analysis progresses. Planned outputs include:
• Ranked diagnostic-feature table with statistical validation (RQ1)
• Classifier comparison and confusion-matrix evaluation vs. traditional methods (RQ2)
• High-lift association rules and co-occurrence network maps (RQ3)
• Global deposit-density heatmaps and under-explored-region recommendations (RQ4)
Ethical Considerations
• Open-access data only — GCDD, Mindat, USGS-MRDS, and MED; no personal or proprietary
data.
• Transparency and reproducibility — full pipeline is documented and version-controlled.
• Attribution — all data sources are credited; licences respected.
• Responsible interpretation — model outputs support, not replace, expert geological judgement.
Roadmap
• Data integration and harmonisation pipeline
• RQ1diagnostic-feature validation
• RQ2classifier benchmark (> 85% target, SSS validation)
• RQ3association-rule and network outputs
• RQ4global heatmaps and targeting recommendations
• Deployable classification module
